Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?dos:=20Phase=2011=20patch=200054=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?silent-Pixtone-SFX=20fix=20(Shape=20A:=20post-mix=20silence-ski?=
 =?UTF-8?q?p)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wave-34 PLAY5 W34A4 confirmed root cause: SDL/0050's pre-mix
quiescence gate in DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf traps Pixtone SFX
under AUDIO_BACKEND=opl3. Operator heard SFX audibly with
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE=0 (killswitched) but
silence with default gate active.

The bug: SDL/0050 returns *buffer_size=0 when no bound stream has
output data, which makes SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate
(SDL_audio.c:1189) skip the entire mix loop AND PlayDevice for that
iter. But SDL3_mixer's MixerCallback (registered as the bound
output_stream's get-callback at SDL_mixer.c:805) is precisely what
PROPAGATES per-track Pixtone audio into the bound stream. Skipping
the mix loop means MixerCallback never fires, tracks never get
pulled, Pixtone fires never reach the device. Vicious cycle under
AUDIO_BACKEND=opl3 — music goes out-of-band via OPL3 register
writes, the SDL audio stream is perpetually empty pre-mix, gate
fires every iter, SFX is silent for the entire session.

Three options surfaced during pair-investigation with build-qa:
  A — post-mix silence-detect (this patch)
  B — default-flip gate OFF (loses +1.4 fps gain)
  C — backend-aware gate auto-disable (cross-vendor extern read;
      state-flag-fragmentation footgun per
      memory/sdl_pause_api_must_audit_auto_resume_gates.md)

Team-lead arbitrated Shape A over C: self-contained in SDL,
generalizes to any audio activity (not just Pixtone-tagged),
architecturally correct layering (post-mix in PlayDevice vs pre-mix
in GetDeviceBuf — WASAPI's gate-at-GetDeviceBuf precedent doesn't
apply to our cooperative-scheduled DOS backend). 0.2 fps cost vs C
is below fps_replication_probe_required.md's noise floor.

Mechanism (Shape A):
  - GetDeviceBuf becomes trivial: always return staging_buffer with
    *buffer_size unchanged. Mixer-tick runs every iter →
    MixerCallback fires → Pixtone tracks get pulled → samples reach
    bound stream when SFX trigger fires.
  - PlayDevice scans the mixed staging buffer for all-silence
    (bytewise compare against soundblaster_silence_value — 0x00 for
    S16, 0x80 for U8 unsigned; early-exit on first non-silence byte;
    ~1-2 μs for typical 256-4096 byte buffers).
  - If all-silence → skip ring write + SDL_Delay(10) throttle. Ring
    continues to drain via IRQ → consecutive-silent-IRQ counter
    ticks → DSP auto-engage idle-pause fires when threshold met →
    IRQ-5 stops → fps recovered. SAME mechanism as SDL/0050;
    triggered post-mix instead of pre-mix.
  - If non-silence (real audio: Pixtone SFX, direct-stream OGG,
    etc.) → normal ring write path → SFX plays.

Coexistence with prior patches:
  - SDL/0051's atomic-shutdown-bypass at top of GetDeviceBuf is now
    dead code (GetDeviceBuf is trivial). Left in tree as documentation
    of the wrong-layer-fix attempt per pressure_test_tidy_narratives.md.
  - SDL/0053's SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown still applies. Reuses
    g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled flag; semantic shifts from
    "skip GetDeviceBuf quiescence walk" (SDL/0050) to "skip PlayDevice
    silence-detect" (SDL/0054) — semantically-equivalent role
    ("disable the SDL/0050-derived behavior") preserves SDL/0053's
    engine-signaled-shutdown contract. The SDL_Delay(10) moved from
    GetDeviceBuf to PlayDevice's silence-skip branch; iter L L1 freeze
    geometry preserved; SDL/0053 unlocks it identically.
  - SDL/0048 (ForcePause), SDL/0046 (WaitDevice shutdown bail),
    SDL/0038 (DSP auto-resume on ring write): unchanged.

Killswitch hint name retained for user-facing compat:
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE=0 still reverts to
pre-0050 behavior (always-write-to-ring). The OpenDevice log message
updated to reflect Shape A's mechanism.

Predicted fps cost: ~0.2 fps vs SDL/0050 default-ON (mixer-tick CPU
per iter when quiescent: ~10-50 μs × ~86 Hz audio-thread-iter rate);
net ~+1.2 fps vs killswitched. Predictions framed as hypothesis per
perf_predictions_unreliable.md; wave-35 PLAY measurement settles
real cost.

Predicted SFX latency: ~10-12 ms from MIX_PlayTrack call to first
sample on ring (one audio-thread-iter cycle at 22050 mono / 256
frames). Same as the pre-SDL/0050 working path; no perceptible
regression for game SFX.

Validation status:
  - DOSBox-X structural smoke (build-qa Task #19 territory): pending
    on wave-35 binary rebuild
  - Real-HW behavioral smoke (wave-35 PLAY1-PLAY5): the actual gate;
    operator confirmation of SFX audibility under default env-baseline
    (no SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE=0 set) is what
    closes Task #23.

Hot-path cost: bytewise silence scan ~1-2 μs per audio-thread iter;
trivial compared to the mixer tick that just produced the buffer
(~50 μs). Early-exit on first non-silence byte means real-audio iters
detect non-silence in O(1) typical case.

One TU touched (src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c). +169/-98 lines net;
~25 LOC behavioral change; balance is inline reasoning comments per
the wave-33 SDL/0053 docstring density precedent.

Per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md the patch stays workspace-local; not for
upstream.

Companion patches:
  SDL/0050 — DOS GetDeviceBuf quiescence gate (this patch supersedes
             the mechanism; killswitch hint name retained)
  SDL/0051 — atomic-shutdown-bypass (now dead code; left for
             documentation of the wrong-layer-fix attempt)
  SDL/0053 — SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown engine-signal (still applies;
             same flag; updated semantic)
  nxengine-evo/0129 — engine companion to SDL/0053; calls
                       SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown before MIX_DestroyMixer

Cross-reference:
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-34-CONTRACT.md PLAY5 W34A4 H2 result (audible
    SFX with killswitched gate; load-bearing root-cause confirmation)
  - memory/sdl_pause_api_must_audit_auto_resume_gates.md (state-flag-
    fragmentation footgun build-qa C3 would have repeated)
  - memory/pressure_test_tidy_narratives.md (Shape A vs C3 architectural
    layering reasoning)
  - audio_cost_attribution_unknown.md (the ~31 ms unattributed audio
    cost surfaced by W30 ablation that wave-35 Phase 12 instrumentation
    will decompose)
