-       silent-IRQ counter never crosses threshold; idle-pause never fires.
-
-       Iter K IDLEPROB v2 confirmed slot 0048 mechanism works (DSP 0xD5 halts
-       IRQ-5 cleanly) but in-gameplay yield = 0.26 ms because the ring stayed
-       continuously filled. This patch is the missing piece: when audio
-       quiescent, GetDeviceBuf returns buffer_size=0 → audio thread skips
-       PlayDevice → ring drains via IRQ → 4 silent IRQs trip auto-engage →
-       DSP pause → IRQ-5 stops → fps recovered.
-
-       Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE=0 disables
-       the gate (returns staging_buffer unconditionally; pre-0050 behavior).
-       Iter L PLAY2 (control) sets this env var; PLAY1 (treatment) leaves
-       unset. Within-iter PLAY1−PLAY2 = SDL/0050 isolation signal.
-
-       The SDL_Delay(10) inside the gate path throttles audio thread to
-       ~100 iter/sec when quiescent, preventing CPU spin under cooperative
-       scheduler when main thread is also time-blocked. */
-    if (!g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled && device->logical_devices != NULL) {
-        bool any_data = false;
-        SDL_LogicalAudioDevice *logdev = device->logical_devices;
-        while (logdev != NULL && !any_data) {
-            SDL_AudioStream *stream = logdev->bound_streams;
-            while (stream != NULL) {
