+       where silence-detection happens AFTER the mixer-tick runs.
+
+       Why Shape A replaces SDL/0050's pre-mix gate:
+
+       SDL/0050 (the patch this supersedes) implemented a pre-mix gate
+       here — return buffer_size=0 when no bound stream had output data,
+       so SDL3 (`SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate`, SDL_audio.c:1189-1295)
+       would skip the entire mix loop AND PlayDevice for that iter. The
+       gate successfully halved the audio path's wall-clock cost (+1.4
+       fps measured per W30A1-vs-W30A2 wave-30 ablation), BUT it had a
+       load-bearing bug surfaced by wave-34 PLAY5 W34A4:
+
+       SDL3_mixer's `MixerCallback` (registered on the mixer's
+       output_stream via SDL_SetAudioStreamGetCallback at
+       SDL_mixer.c:805) is what PROPAGATES per-track Pixtone audio into
+       the bound output stream. With buffer_size=0, SDL3 skips the mix
+       loop's `SDL_GetAudioStreamDataAdjustGain` call → MixerCallback
+       never fires → tracks never get pulled → Pixtone fires never
+       reach the device. Under AUDIO_BACKEND=opl3 (music routed
+       out-of-band via OPL3 register writes; SDL audio stream perpetually
+       empty pre-mix), the gate fires every iter; SFX is silent for the
+       entire session.
+
+       Wave-34 H2 BAT cell confirmed root-cause: operator heard SFX
+       audibly under `SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE=0`
+       (killswitched gate; pre-0050 behavior) but silence with the
+       default gate active.
+
+       Shape A retains the +1.4 fps gain mechanism (DSP auto-engage
+       idle-pause when ring drains) by moving the gate logic from
